== Complete physical comparison and exact weights

The replay analyzer forms a complete neutral key from interaction rule IDs, labelled sewn external roles, directed particle edges, and parallel edge occurrences. It enumerates remaining node and edge permutations, counts directed automorphisms independently, maps original node/edge IDs to the representative, and maps initial-state, selected physical-cut, and threshold-candidate half-edge incidence. Every filtered and zero-color-off physical key is unique per route; all corresponding keys, cut maps, raw factors, evaluated weights, and graph-derived signs match historical/current. Selected physical cuts are verified as full half-edge partitions with exactly paired crossing incidence. Topology-threshold candidates may cover a proper subgraph; the corrected checker verifies unique, exactly paired crossings within that selected subgraph while preserving omitted outside regions. It also checks one incoming and one outgoing Grassmann arrow at every internal vertex of open chains and source/sink external roles from the live model. The original seven controls and 33 round2 controls reject corruptions and accept valid graph relabellings, complete ghost-circuit reversal, and equivalent scalar spelling.

For each graph, the independently checked scalar weight is `(-1)^(closed quark loops + closed ghost loops) * external-ordering sign * incoming-antifermion spin-sum sign / directed AutG`. In the electron/positron row the two external signs are each `-1`, so their product is `+1`; in the photon row both are `+1`. Vacuum graphs have no external legs, retain the trivial `ExternalFermionOrderingSign(1)` head, and have no `AntiFermionSpinSumSign` head. There is no grouping or extra cut-direction factor in these raw overall-factor expressions. The corrected analyzer consumes the complete TSV and qualified DOT scalar expressions with a bounded grammar and exact BigInt rationals, checking both independently against their recorded evaluated values and the graph-derived factors. The external Grassmann chains and sewn endpoint closure, directed loop flow, ghost/quark particle spins, and parallel-edge automorphisms come from physical DOT and the live model. No graph numerator is expanded.

